law.text:
		Within 15 days of becoming aware of the occurrence of any of the events listed below, a licensee shall file a written report with the Commissioner describing such event:

The institution of revocation or suspension proceedings against the licensee by any state or other governmental authority;


The denial of the opportunity to engage in business by any state or other governmental authority;


Any felony indictment of the licensee;


Any felony conviction of the licensee; and


Such other events as the Commission may determine and identify by regulation.
